    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "No strategic_frame.json exists for this deck; the engine reading came from CONTEXT.md (Meren attrition, win on a count of deaths with drains).",
      "No region carries a verified_count above zero: no rules-verified line touches this list yet, so no city is the engine on the record.",
      "The drain package is split three ways by card type, which reads as CardBERT clustering on type over function: Zulaport Cutthroat and Blood Artist in THE SMALL DEATHS, Starscape Cleric (the multiplier per CONTEXT.md) in THE MUSCLE, Grave Venerations, The Meathook Massacre and Boggart Mischief in DEATH PAYS.",
      "city-6 has a single neighbourhood with identical membership (all seven enchantments); it is left unnamed because any name would repeat its parent.",
      "city-0-hood-0 mixes four tutors with three catch-all answers (Assassin's Trophy, Beast Within, Trystan's Command); named FIND OR FIX for the two jobs visible, the join is the any-target flexibility, not a shared role.",
      "city-1-hood-1 (Garruk's Uprising, Icetill Explorer, Ribtruss Roaster) is three unrelated green engines -- card draw on big bodies, lands from the graveyard, token growth; the split from the parent looks arbitrary.",
      "city-2-hood-0 is mostly bodies that return or pay on entry (Graveshifter, Scrapwork Rager, Teacher's Pest, Dawnhand Eulogist); Obelisk Spider is the odd member, a -1/-1 counter drain that fits better beside the drains in SAC, DIE, DRAIN.",
      "city-3 splits the two altars by what they make, not what they do: Ashnod's Altar sits with Sol Ring (two colourless), Phyrexian Altar with Arcane Signet and Chrome Mox (coloured). Both are sac outlets functionally closer to THE SMALL DEATHS than to rocks.",
      "city-3-hood-0 is 19 any-colour lands in a two-colour deck, almost all of them conditional (pay {1}, life, or a creature); that mass is a shape worth noticing, though judging it is not this agent's job.",
      "Phyrexian Tower sits among the untapped duals in ON-TIME DUALS but is a free sacrifice outlet that makes {B}{B}; it is the most engine-relevant land in HOME SOIL.",
      "city-5-hood-0 is lands that enter tapped or conditionally tapped; Boseiju, Who Endures (untapped, a channel answer) is the odd member.",
      "Supernatural Stamina has no role tag; in KILL AND RAISE it is a self-recursion trick, which matches the neighbourhood's reanimation half."
    ]
  },
